OL,3,GNEWSA1960s 'police box' in city centre
OL,4,Aopens to public
OL,5,
OL,6,FA mint-green police box used by
OL,7,Fofficers as a "mini station" to make
OL,8,Fcalls and file paperwork until the
OL,9,F1960s has been opened to the public.
OL,11,FThe box, built in 1928, is located on
OL,12,FSurrey Street in Sheffield and was one
OL,13,Fof 120 dotted around the city. They
OL,14,Falso had blue electric lamp on top,
OL,15,Fwhich stations could light up to signal
OL,16,Fthat an officer on patrol needed to
OL,17,Fanswer the phone for an urgent message.
OL,19,FAs part of Heritage Open Days, the box
OL,20,Fis open until Saturday alongside a
OL,21,Fvintage Morris Minor police car and
OL,22,Fvarious policing items from that era.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
